WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
Welcome to Planetarian Daily, episode 116.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.280
Today is July 10th, 2026.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.300
Let's get into today's research and health developments.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.780
Modified low-protein Mediterranean diet helped mice eat more

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:16.080
while losing fat and reducing frailty.

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.700
Researchers tested a low-protein version of the diet

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.700
that retained enough methionine on laboratory mice.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.520
The animals consumed more calories yet showed lower body fat,

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:31.520
reduced frailty, and extended health span compared with controls.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:38.720
Human observational data in the same report linked lower animal protein intake to reduced obesity

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:45.180
and type 2 diabetes rates. The mechanism appears tied to altered amino acid signaling that

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:48.600
favors fat oxidation without restricting total energy.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:54.680
Follow-up work will test whether similar macronutrient ratios produce measurable benefits in

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:00.340
human metabolic trials. A few episodes back the show covered cellular aging interventions,

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:06.360
and today's mouse data adds a dietary route that shifts metabolism without calorie restriction.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:12.540
The low-protein Mediterranean-style diet allowed mice to eat more calories while losing fat

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:18.060
and showing less frailty. The benefit appears linked to restricted methionine availability,

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:24.240
which shifts metabolism toward fat oxidation. Human cohort data in the same study

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:29.960
already associate lower animal protein intake with reduced obesity and diabetes prevalence.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:36.220
Next, controlled human feeding trials will determine whether the same macronutrient balance produces

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:42.800
comparable metabolic shifts without compromising nutrient adequacy. What dietary variable would you

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:48.840
most want tested in a follow-up human study? Now shifting to a study that corrects a long-standing

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:55.240
assumption about animal behavior and human safety. A new study directly measured venom yield and

00:01:55.240 --> 00:02:01.620
composition across age classes in multiple rattlesnake species. Young snakes delivered controlled

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:07.880
amounts comparable to adults, while adult bites injected substantially larger volumes and produced

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:14.660
more severe clinical effects. The team traced the more dangerous juveniles claim to repeated inaccuracies

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:21.220
in decades of news coverage rather than primary data. The finding corrects a widespread public safety

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:27.220
misconception that has influenced first aid guidance. Now here's something most people get wrong.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.200
Most people assume baby rattlesnakes are more dangerous because they cannot control how much venom

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:39.400
they inject. In reality, young snakes meter venom with the same precision as adults. Right now,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:45.740
as you consider outdoor safety, the key variable is not age but the absolute volume delivered.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:52.780
Adults routinely inject far larger amounts producing more severe bites. A memorable figure from

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:58.540
the study is that adult bites delivered substantially higher venom loads than juvenile ones across

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:05.000
multiple species. The practical takeaway is to treat every rattlesnake encounter with the same caution

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:10.660
regardless of size and to ignore outdated first aid advice that singles out juveniles.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:17.200
University of Michigan researchers tracked morning glory populations over nine years under rising

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:23.320
temperatures and falling pollinator numbers. Plants shifted investment toward floral traits that

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:30.120
attract remaining pollinators. This change cut the rate of climate-related adaptation by 96%.

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:36.220
Repeated measures of selection gradients on leaf and flowering traits documented the trade off.

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:42.340
Agricultural weeds and crops may face comparable evolutionary constraints when pollinators decline.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:48.280
The nine-year data set captured both temperature increases and pollinator losses in the same

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:54.300
populations. Selection pressures redirected resources away from thermal adaptation traits.

00:03:55.240 --> 00:04:02.100
NeuroVFM was trained on standard clinical MRI and CT examinations collected across a health system.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:08.560
The model produces representations that improve diagnostic accuracy, automated report generation

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:15.260
and triage decisions from multiple neurological conditions. Performance gains held across scanner

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:21.360
vendors and patient populations not seen during training. The approach demonstrates how existing

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:26.880
private imaging archives can be repurposed for safer, more generalizable medical AI.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:33.540
Training drew exclusively from routine hospital scans rather than curated research data sets.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:39.580
The resulting embedding support tasks spanning several neurological conditions simultaneously.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:47.680
Researchers modified adenosine dMNAs acting on RNA to act on DNA while minimizing bystander edits

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:54.180
at nearby adenines. The engineered enzymes were tested across multiple genomic low-key in cell

00:04:54.180 --> 00:05:00.740
culture, showing high on-target efficiency with sharply reduced off-target activity. The system

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:07.400
expands the base editing toolbox beyond current cytosine and adenine editors. Next steps include

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:14.020
delivery optimization for in vivo applications. Tests covered several distinct genomic sites to

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:20.080
assess consistency. Off-target reduction occurred without loss of overall editing efficiency.

00:05:20.660 --> 00:05:26.800
A new formulation pairs cytosine base editors with uracil DNA glycosolase inhibitors

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:32.840
delivered via virus-like particles. The combination produced efficient editing in mouse liver

00:05:32.840 --> 00:05:38.800
and other tissues while limiting in-del formation. Glycosolase inhibition prevents

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.980
excision of the edited base, raising conversion rates without increasing DNA damage.

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:48.020
The platform is being evaluated for additional tissue targets.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:53.400
Virus-like particles carried both the editor and the inhibitor components together.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:57.540
Editing outcomes were measured in liver and extra-hypatic tissues.

00:05:58.240 --> 00:06:05.660
The structure of the type IF-3 cast transposase TNSB bound to left and right transposon ends,

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:12.400
shows the distortions required to accommodate sequence asymmetry. Molecular dynamics simulations

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:17.560
indicate these distortions enable coordinated assembly of the paired end complex.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:23.940
Mutational analysis confirmed that the resulting protein-protein interface is necessary for

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:30.380
efficient transposition. The finding supply design rules for engineering cast systems to carry larger

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:38.960
DNA cargoes. CryoEM captured the transposase in its DNA-bound state. Simulations revealed how end

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:45.260
asymmetry is accommodated during complex formation. A hybrid quantum classical generative model

00:06:45.260 --> 00:06:50.880
sampled latent vectors from a photonic quantum processor to seed peptide sequences.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:58.560
Across 131 HLA alleles, quantum priors increased the fraction of predicted strong binders,

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:05.280
with largest gains for alleles that had limited training data. In vitro ELISA validation on three

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:11.420
understudied alleles confirmed that quantum design peptides stabilized peptide MHC complexes

00:07:11.420 --> 00:07:17.420
more effectively than classical baselines. The method offers a route to personalized vaccine

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:23.520
and immunotherapy antigens. The photonic processor generated initial sequence distributions.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:28.020
Validation focused on alleles with sparse prior data coverage.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:34.620
A standard proteomics spin tip retains peptides after digestion while allowing genomic DNA

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:41.560
to pass into the flow through. When combined with deep visual proteomics, the approach yields matched

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:46.600
genome and proteome profiles from the same cells in archival melanoma samples.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:52.640
The method works on formal and fixed paraffin embedded material without specialized equipment.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:59.160
It opens cell type resolved mutation proteome studies in existing clinical bio banks.

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:06.420
DNA flows through while peptides remain captured on the tip. Archival melanoma specimens provided

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:12.500
the matched profiles. Advanced interferometric observations revealed organized drift patterns

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:19.160
in cold, dense gas concentrations that precede star formation. The measurements resolved velocity

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:25.680
fields on scales previously inaccessible, showing how gravity and turbulence interact inside these

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:31.720
cores. The data constrain models of the earliest stages of solar type star formation.

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:37.160
Continued monitoring will test whether similar flows appear in cores of different masses.

00:08:37.960 --> 00:08:43.920
Radio telescope arrays captured the internal motions. Drift patterns emerged at scales smaller

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:50.340
than prior observations allowed. Dental wear and isotopic analyses of homo-flora z-seang

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:57.240
remains indicated diet heavy on scavenged large animal carcasses. The pattern differs from expectations

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:03.100
for active hunting and suggests the species may have occupied a distinct ecological niche on the

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:09.480
island. The findings re-open questions about the timing and route of hominin arrival in southeast

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:15.980
Asia. Additional fossils will be needed to confirm whether this foraging strategy persisted across the

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:21.280
species range. Wear patterns on teeth aligned with scavenging rather than hunting.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:28.200
Isotopic signatures matched consumption of large animal remains. Brown University chemists

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:33.140
synthesized and characterized molecules containing carbon bismuth triple bonds.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:39.180
Spectroscopic and computational data show that relativistic effects blur the textbook

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:45.720
distinction between sigma and pi components. The work provides the first direct experimental evidence

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:52.220
that periodic table trends in bonding change qualitatively for the heaviest elements. Similar effects

00:09:52.220 --> 00:09:58.240
are now being explored in other super heavy element systems. The synthesized compounds featured

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:04.240
carbon bismuth linkages. Relativistic contributions altered expected bond character.

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:10.840
University of Ottawa researchers shaped laser light to replicate particle dynamics in complex

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:17.840
materials. The optical simulator reproduce transport behavior across hundreds of distinct Hamiltonians

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:23.820
without requiring larger electronic circuits. Validation against numerical models confirmed

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:30.400
quantitative agreement for both localized and delocalized regimes. The platform offers a compact

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:36.200
test bed for materials that are difficult to fabricate or measure directly. Laser beam shaping

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:42.260
encoded the target Hamiltonians. Hundreds of different transport scenarios were tested optically.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:48.700
A university at Buffalo team applied quantum optics methods to enhance visibility of a subtle

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:54.860
interference pattern generated inside the eye. The amplified signal could serve as a non-invasive

00:10:54.860 --> 00:11:01.200
indicator of retinal health. Early tests in human volunteers showed the pattern could be recorded

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:07.500
with standard ophthalmic hardware once the quantum illumination was applied. Larger clinical studies

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:13.280
are planned to correlate signal strength with known retinal diseases. Quantum illumination

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:19.580
boosted the otherwise faint interference signal. Volunteer recordings used unmodified clinical

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:26.160
instruments after illumination. Laboratory modeling of a synchronously rotating planet showed that

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:31.340
interior heat can circulate in a stable loop between the permanent day and night sides.

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:37.560
The circulation creates latitude bands where surface temperatures remain within liquid water ranges

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:44.300
despite extreme stellar irradiation contrasts. The result expands the set of orbital configurations

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:51.220
considered potentially habitable. Future atmospheric observations will test whether such heat redistribution

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:57.940
occurs on real exoplanets. Modeling focused on tidally locked rotation states. Heat flow

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:04.040
establish stable temperate latitude zones. Keep an eye on follow-up human feeding trials that will

00:12:04.040 --> 00:12:10.620
test the low-protein Mediterranean macronutrient ratios in metabolic studies. That's planetarian

